<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified" attributeFormDefault="unqualified">

	<xs:annotation>
		<xs:documentation>
		</xs:documentation>
	</xs:annotation>

	<xs:include schemaLocation="rest_linking_parameters.xsd"/>
	
	<xs:element name="group_settings" type="group_settings"/>

	<xs:complexType name="group_settings">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>List of access restrictions based on locations.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="group_setting" type="group_setting" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo>
						<xs:tags>api get post put</xs:tags>
					</xs:appinfo>
					<xs:documentation>Access restrictions based on location.
					</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>			
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>		
	
	<xs:complexType name="group_setting">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Access restrictions based on location.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
		<xs:element name="group" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo>
						<xs:tags>api get post put</xs:tags>
						<xs:example/>
					</xs:appinfo>
					<xs:documentation>Group name. Must be a valid [Inventory Management Group|http://knowledge.exlibrisgroup.com/Alma/Product_Documentation/Alma_Online_Help_(English)/Resource_Management/080Configuring_Resource_Management/160Configuring_Inventory_Management_Groups].
						The "desc" attribute contains the group description.
					</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:complexType>
					<xs:simpleContent>
						<xs:extension base="xs:string">
							<xs:attribute name="desc" type="xs:string"/>
						</xs:extension>
					</xs:simpleContent>
				</xs:complexType>
			</xs:element>			
		<xs:element name="proxy_enabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo>
						<!-- <xs:codeTable>GroupProxyEnabled</xs:codeTable>  -->
						<xs:tags>api get post put</xs:tags>
						<xs:example>0</xs:example>
					</xs:appinfo>
					<xs:documentation>Whether to enable a proxy.
					Possible code are listed in GroupProxyEnabled [code table|https://developers.exlibrisgroup.com/blog/Working-with-the-code-tables-API]
					with one exception:  "Resource Default" is returned as an empty field instead of "2".
					In the PUT action, proxy_enabled can be modified for all collections.
					</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:complexType>
					<xs:simpleContent>
						<xs:extension base="xs:string">
							<xs:attribute name="desc" type="xs:string"/>
						</xs:extension>
					</xs:simpleContent>
				</xs:complexType>
			</xs:element>	

			<xs:element name="proxy" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo>
						<xs:tags>api get post put</xs:tags>
						<xs:example>LAW_PROXY</xs:example>
					</xs:appinfo>
					<xs:documentation>A proxy profile code. This must be a valid code of an integration profile of "Resolver proxy" type.
					In the PUT action, proxy can be modified for all collections.
					</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>				
			<xs:element name="public_name" type="xs:string" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo>
						<xs:tags>api get post put</xs:tags>
						<xs:example/>
					</xs:appinfo>
					<xs:documentation>The name to display in the discovery search results. Mandatory.
					In the PUT action, public_name can be modified only for local collections.
					</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			
			<xs:element name="authentication_note" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo>
						<xs:tags>api get post put</xs:tags>
						<xs:example/>
					</xs:appinfo>
					<xs:documentation>A note related to authentication (to display in the discovery system).
					In the PUT action, authentication_note can be modified for all collections.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>

			<xs:element name="public_note" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo>
						<xs:tags>api get post put</xs:tags>
						<xs:example/>
					</xs:appinfo>
					<xs:documentation>Information about the service (to display in the discovery system.)
					In the PUT action, public_note can be modified for all collections.
					</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>

			<xs:element name="linking_parameters" type="linking_parameters" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo>
						<xs:tags>api get post put</xs:tags>
					</xs:appinfo>
					<xs:documentation>The group_settings related linking parameters. Parameters are inherited from the service, values are set on the group_settings level. In the PUT action the incoming list will replace the existing list. If linking_parameters element is not part of the payload, or exists in the payload but is empty, the existing list will be deleted.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>

			<xs:element name="access_model" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo>
						<xs:tags>api get post put</xs:tags>
						<xs:example/>
					</xs:appinfo>
					<xs:documentation>A code representing resource availability for simultaneous use. This element is optional, but if it contains a non-null value, it must be a valid code existing in both of the [Access Model code tables|https://knowledge.exlibrisgroup.com/Alma/Product_Documentation/010Alma_Online_Help_(English)/020Acquisitions/110Configuring_Acquisitions/310Managing_Access_Models].
					In the PUT action, access_model can be modified for all collections.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>			
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>		
</xs:schema>